{
  "$comment": [
    "#2148 Stage 3 [ci-runtime]. Registry of per-issue suites that each used to be",
    "their own CI job. MEASURED on a real PR: the non-database CI set spent 60",
    "job-minutes running tests and 65 job-minutes setting up to run them; a typical",
    "per-issue job burned ~40s of checkout and runner boot for ~14s of node --test.",
    "With the org capped at 20 concurrent jobs that PR queued 335 job-minutes against",
    "141 spent executing. This deletes the setup, not the tests.",
    "",
    "run-suite-batch.mjs iterates THIS FILE and never a glob. A glob would turn a",
    "deleted or renamed suite into a silent skip and a green run into a lie. It asserts",
    "executed === expectedSuites, so losing a suite fails the run on its own. Same",
    "contract as ORCH-1383's run-batch.mjs, which replaced 340 one-gate jobs.",
    "",
    "TWO THINGS DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED, both discovered by measuring rather than",
    "assuming:",
    "  * SELF-PINNED suites. 118 files in this repo read a .github/workflows/*.yml and",
    "    assert their own suite is wired there \u2014 the anti-dark-gate discipline #2113",
    "    exists for. Folding those in deletes the file they assert on and breaks them,",
    "    so all 33 such candidates keep their own workflow. Batching them requires",
    "    repointing those assertions at this manifest, which edits test files and needs",
    "    explicit approval.",
    "  * Suites using an action beyond checkout/setup-node (setup-python, k6-action).",
    "    The batch runs shell steps only, so folding them in would silently drop their",
    "    setup. The generator refuses them by name rather than guessing.",
    "",
    "CLASSES ARE DEPENDENCY PROFILES, not arbitrary shards, so each class pays exactly",
    "one install for all its suites.",
    "",
    "These suites now run on EVERY pull request; their old workflows were paths-gated.",
    "That is MORE coverage, not less \u2014 a paths-gated suite silently skips on a PR that",
    "misses its globs, which is how a latent main-red landed in PR #743 and surfaced on",
    "an unrelated PR. originPaths is retained per suite as provenance only.",
    "  * Workflows PROVIDING A REQUIRED STATUS CHECK. framework-major-guard.yml was",
    "    caught here: its job name 'Framework Major Guard' is required by ruleset",
    "    19508605. Folding it in deletes the check name, it never reports, and EVERY",
    "    PR in the repo blocks forever on a check that no longer exists. Verify any",
    "    candidate against the rulesets' required_status_checks before batching it.",
    "",
    "TO ADD a suite: add it here. TO REMOVE one: you must also lower expectedSuites,",
    "which is a visible, reviewable act. There is no token that removes a suite quietly.",
    "",
    "job that would become the new critical path \u2014 a regression, since today they run",
    "suite-results.json precisely so the shards can be rebalanced from evidence after",
    "the first CI run rather than guessed at again.",
    "  * Suites pinned by .github/scripts/strict-grep/MANIFEST.json. It names workflows",
    "    as `external:<file>.yml` with no directory prefix, so a scan for the literal",
    "    string '.github/workflows/<file>.yml' MISSES them \u2014 orch-1386-tester-adversarial",
    "    slipped through that way and failed META-1383 parity check P4. Check BOTH the",
    "    `external:` field and `jobKeys` before batching anything.",
    "",
    "SHARDING IS BIN-PACKED FROM MEASURED COST, not by counting suites. The 14 business",
    "suites are far from equal (113s and 98s at the top, 35s at the bottom, 673s total),",
    "so an even split by count would leave one shard setting the critical path alone.",
    "carries per-suite seconds, so re-run this packing whenever suites are added.",
    "",
    "SHARDS ARE BIN-PACKED FROM CI-MEASURED COST. Local timings were NOT usable: the",
    "same suites ranked differently on a runner, and the first CI run came out at",
    "5.9/4.5/3.6/4.3 min against a local prediction of ~3 min each. Local evidence",
    "proves equivalence, never timing.",
    "There is a HARD FLOOR here: issue-1027 alone is 170s on CI, so no shard can go",
    "below ~4.2 min however many ways this is split. Adding shards past 4 buys nothing",
    "and costs a fresh npm ci (~80s) each."
  ],
  "expectedSuites": 21,
